          "short": "$(1,-6),(2,-4)$; gradient $2$.",
          "worked": "At $x=1$, $y=-6$; at $x=2$, $y=-4$. Thus $$\\begin{aligned}m&=\\frac{-4-(-6)}{2-1}\\\\&=2\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
